WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.138
Luke Cage: "My Name is Luke Cage."

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:13.179
If you're like me and you binge-watched all thirteen episodes of Luke Cage, your brain is probably mush. 

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:16.516
Along with forgetting to feed yourself, you probably missed these references. 

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.686
Here are our top five favorite easter eggs from Luke Cage. 

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.355
Number 5: Stan Lee's Cameo

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:26.493
Lee's face can be seen on a poster in the twelfth episode opf Luke Cage. 

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.629
When Luke stop a robbery and runs into Method Man. 

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.197
There you see Stan, 

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:35.969
Dressed as a police officer, urging citizens to report any crimes they may see. 

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:39.172
Also, Luke and Method swap sweatshirts. 

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.540
Besties! 

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.176
Number 4: Colleen Wing

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:48.748
In episode thirteen, Claire Temple finds a flier for Martial arts training by Colleen Wing.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.786
 In the Comics, Colleen is Misty Knight’s partner in Heroes for Hire,

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.687
a group started by Luke Cage. 

00:00:54.687 --> 00:01:00.093
She is also friends with Luke Cage’s partner and the next Marvel hero to get his own show,

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.629
Danny Rand, or Iron Fist. 

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.365
Number Three: Power Man 

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:11.271
Power Man is the moniker Luke Cage decides to go by after being in the hero game for a while 

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.673
and realizing he needs to up his brand.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:18.578
Pop calls him this in what sounds like an inside joke. We get it Pop. 

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.981
Pop: "Not a problem for you, Power Man"

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.184
Number Two:  Back to the Future

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:28.188
In Episode 10, Misty Knight is looking at microfiche (I love that word) newspaper records

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:32.058
or Carl Lucas, Luke Cage’s name from before he gained powers.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:36.262
She finds the article she needs and the article we all want. 

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:40.533
An obvious homage to Back to the Future with changes to prevent copyright issues.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:46.806
Martian Brown and Mac Fly are referenced as well as a “Thrust Capacitor”. 

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:52.512
Dr. Brown: "Roads? Where we're going we don't need roads."

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.982
Number One: The Classic Cage Costume

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.418
This is an obvious one for comic book readers. 

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:03.056
After escaping from Seagate Prison with his fashionable tiara and cuffs,

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.159
Cage comes across a baggy yellow shirt.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.828
It's a wierd moment for comic book readers.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:13.700
Cage looks at his reflection for 30 seconds and realizes what we've all known for 30 years. 

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.301
He looks rediculous. 

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.104
Luke Cage: "You look like a damn fool."

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:21.708
Sometimes the comic books just don’t translate to the screen but

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.777
kudos to the producers for throwing it in there for us.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:30.450
